       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's long half-life would make the effects last a long time. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n- **A typo or wrong dose.** The usual dosing is 2.5 to 5 mg once daily to start, and up to 10 mg once daily. If you meant 5 mg, tell me and I'll enter it right away. The same goes for 10 mg or 2.5 mg.\n- **A deliberate 50 mg dose.** If this is intentional, for example under a specialist's direction, tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though I'd recommend confirming with pharmacy first.\n\nWhich dose should I enter?"
      }
